  "days_covered": 1,
  "primer": {
    "text": "Ethiopia and Eritrea are two states in the Horn of Africa, and Tigray is a region within Ethiopia where Ethiopian government forces and Tigray-aligned forces have contested control. Mekelle is the main city in Tigray and the location of its airport, so control of the airport signals control of the regional center. A rupture in relations between Ethiopia and Eritrea and intensified fighting inside Tigray are understood as one escalation because the interstate relationship and the internal contest over Tigray affect each other, with implications for security across the Horn.",
    "built_at": "2026-10-04T07:26:06.472952+00:00"
  },
  "current": {
    "date": "2026-10-03",
    "bottom_line": "Ethiopia and Eritrea severed diplomatic ties on Oct 1 in a tit-for-tat embassy closure and expulsions, ending the 2018 rapprochement as fighting in Tigray intensified. On Oct 3 federal forces likely retook Mekelle's Alula Aba Nega Airport as TPLF fighters pulled back from the city, suggesting a battlefield reversal after TPLF gains on Sept 23, but telecom blackouts prevent independent verification. The rupture has already widened to Egypt and brought explosions to Addis Ababa, raising interstate war risk in the Horn.",
